# Definition of Done

## Purpose

One shared checklist so features, reviews, and releases agree on "done" without bloating always-on context.

## When Applied

Request when a change is feature-complete, under review, or being released (Orchestrator, Reviewer, QA, Release, Documentation). Not glob-scoped.

## Requirements

A change is done when:

- Boundaries hold: remote I/O in data layer, UI via `AuthenticatedShell`, DI registered in `lib/core/di/injection.dart`.
- DB impact is stated: RLS and `SECURITY DEFINER` surface called out; `supabase/*.sql` updated if schema changed.
- Cache behavior preserved: cache-first emit + revalidate, invalidation via existing sync helpers.
- Tests cover new repo/BLoC behavior (see [`quality/testing.mdc`](../quality/testing.mdc)).
- Docs/memory updated when behavior changed (see [`quality/documentation.mdc`](../quality/documentation.mdc)).
- Scope respected (see [`01-change-discipline.mdc`](01-change-discipline.mdc)).

## Examples

- PR summary lists: files touched, RLS/RPC impact, cache keys invalidated, tests added.

## Anti-patterns

- Merging without stating RLS/RPC implications for a DB-touching change.

## Common Mistakes

- "Works on my device" with no test and no cache-invalidation check.
- Behavior changed but `ai/memory/` and `docs/` left stale.
